      "sourceHash": "aee9dcadc76b6e434b408e1f400f4af43e098d269b61036e6cd854ba38b77b9d",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.57,
          "end": 4.08,
          "en": "Now before we explore the other ways",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.08,
          "end": 7.86,
          "en": "of building Angular apps, which can help us get rid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.86,
          "end": 10.56,
          "en": "of the disadvantages I mentioned before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.56,
          "end": 12.81,
          "en": "I, first of all want to show you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.81,
          "end": 16.83,
          "en": "how you could deploy this application here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.83,
          "end": 21.09,
          "en": "how you could deploy this single page application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.09,
          "end": 22.86,
          "en": "And as mentioned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.86,
          "end": 27,
          "en": "you just need a static web host for that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27,
          "end": 29.91,
          "en": "So if you search for static web host,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.91,
          "end": 33.48,
          "en": "you'll find plenty of hosting providers that offer you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.48,
          "end": 37.083,
          "en": "just that static web hosting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.01,
          "end": 41.22,
          "en": "Now, one provider, which I like quite a bit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 41.22,
          "end": 44.85,
          "en": "for hosting static web apps is Firebase,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.85,
          "end": 47.55,
          "en": "which is a service offered by Google,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.55,
          "end": 51.03,
          "en": "but you can of course use any service you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.03,
          "end": 54.42,
          "en": "The great thing about Firebase is that you can get started",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54.42,
          "end": 56.79,
          "en": "with hosting for free though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.79,
          "end": 61.79,
          "en": "All you need to do is log in with your Google account",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 62.25,
          "end": 64.923,
          "en": "and then go to the Firebase console.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 65.85,
          "end": 69.45,
          "en": "There, you then want to create a new project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 69.45,
          "end": 71.25,
          "en": "and give it any name of your choice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 71.25,
          "end": 73.98,
          "en": "like ng-deployment example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 73.98,
          "end": 76.53,
          "en": "but the name is up to you, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 76.53,
          "end": 80.07300000000001,
          "en": "You then must accept the terms and check this box.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 82.35,
          "end": 83.52,
          "en": "And on the next page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 83.52,
          "end": 86.13,
          "en": "we can actually disable Google Analytics here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 86.13,
          "end": 88.8,
          "en": "We don't need that for this demo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 88.8,
          "end": 91.47,
          "en": "And that will then get a Firebase started",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 91.47,
          "end": 93.363,
          "en": "with the project set up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.22999999999999,
          "end": 96.42,
          "en": "Now, Firebase is a service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 96.42,
          "end": 99.6,
          "en": "that offers much more than just hosting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 99.6,
          "end": 103.62,
          "en": "You could also use a database offered by Firebase",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 103.62,
          "end": 106.97999999999999,
          "en": "to connect it to your web application if you were building",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 106.97999999999999,
          "end": 108.63,
          "en": "a more complex application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 108.63,
          "end": 110.85,
          "en": "So you can definitely also explore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 110.85,
          "end": 112.25999999999999,
          "en": "those other offerings.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 112.25999999999999,
          "end": 115.41,
          "en": "Here, I only care about the hosting though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 115.41,
          "end": 120.41,
          "en": "So with that project created, we can go to this build",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 120.81,
          "end": 123.663,
          "en": "area here on the left and choose hosting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 126.48,
          "end": 129.3,
          "en": "And there, you'll then find all the steps you need to go",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 129.3,
          "end": 133.08,
          "en": "through to host an application with Firebase,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 133.08,
          "end": 137.403,
          "en": "a static application, a static website as it says here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 139.2,
          "end": 140.82,
          "en": "So click on get started.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 140.82,
          "end": 142.38,
          "en": "And then as a first step,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 142.38,
          "end": 145.8,
          "en": "we must install this tool here on our system,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 145.8,
          "end": 148.023,
          "en": "this Firebase CLI.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 149.34,
          "end": 153.09,
          "en": "So in my terminal, I'll run this command.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 153.09,
          "end": 156.36,
          "en": "And on Mac OS and Linux, you might need to add sudo",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 156.36,
          "end": 158.463,
          "en": "in front of this to make it work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 160.05,
          "end": 164.07,
          "en": "So this will now install the Firebase CLI on our system,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 164.07,
          "end": 168.27,
          "en": "which we will need in order to use Firebase in this project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 168.27,
          "end": 172.053,
          "en": "and to connect this application to a Firebase project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 174.69,
          "end": 178.86,
          "en": "So with that finished, we can move on to the next step",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 178.86,
          "end": 182.04,
          "en": "and then run this command here to log in with",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 182.04,
          "end": 184.53,
          "en": "that Firebase CLI.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 184.53,
          "end": 188.55,
          "en": "So that's what I'll do, run Firebase login.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 188.55,
          "end": 191.73,
          "en": "And once you did that, you are ready for the next step,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 191.73,
          "end": 194.55,
          "en": "which is to initialize your local project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 194.55,
          "end": 198.12,
          "en": "as a Firebase project, which simply means that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 198.12,
          "end": 200.43,
          "en": "some configuration files will be added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 200.43,
          "end": 203.523,
          "en": "and a link to the Firebase project will be set up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 204.66,
          "end": 206.67000000000002,
          "en": "So if you run Firebase in it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 206.67000000000002,
          "end": 209.34,
          "en": "you'll be asked a couple of questions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 209.34,
          "end": 212.493,
          "en": "For example, which Firebase features you want to use?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 213.39,
          "end": 216.09,
          "en": "And as mentioned, there are many features you could use,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 216.09,
          "end": 219.09,
          "en": "but here I only need the hosting feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 219.09,
          "end": 224.09,
          "en": "So I'll navigate to hosting and use space to activate this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 225.24,
          "end": 226.59300000000002,
          "en": "and then hit enter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 228,
          "end": 231.3,
          "en": "Next, I'll choose use an existing project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 231.3,
          "end": 234.6,
          "en": "because I already created a project on Firebase,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 234.6,
          "end": 235.68,
          "en": "which I want to use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 235.68,
          "end": 238.29,
          "en": "So this now refers to Firebase projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 238.29,
          "end": 240.063,
          "en": "not Angular projects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 241.29,
          "end": 243.18,
          "en": "And I'll then select that one project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 243.18,
          "end": 244.683,
          "en": "which I did create before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 246.39,
          "end": 249.84,
          "en": "Now, regarding the build directory,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 249.84,
          "end": 253.11,
          "en": "you should not use the default, which would be public,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 253.11,
          "end": 256.2,
          "en": "but instead point at that browser folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 256.2,
          "end": 258.54,
          "en": "in the dist/routing folder in my case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 258.54,
          "end": 261.03,
          "en": "because it's that folder that contains the files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 261.03,
          "end": 262.98,
          "en": "that should be deployed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 262.98,
          "end": 267.98,
          "en": "So my public directory, here is dist/routing/browser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 270.15,
          "end": 272.13,
          "en": "and with that, I'll hit enter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 272.13,
          "end": 275.67,
          "en": "and then choose Y for this question,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 275.67,
          "end": 279.06,
          "en": "whether I want to configure it as a single page app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 279.06,
          "end": 282.36,
          "en": "Y for yes, because that is what I want to do here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 282.36,
          "end": 285.65999999999997,
          "en": "I only have one single HTML file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 285.65999999999997,
          "end": 288.9,
          "en": "and this is an important setting because otherwise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 288.9,
          "end": 292.71,
          "en": "routing might not work once the app is deployed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 292.71,
          "end": 297.69,
          "en": "Because if a user then sends a request to some domain/tasks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 297.69,
          "end": 301.08,
          "en": "and Firebase doesn't know what to do with that request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 301.08,
          "end": 305.13,
          "en": "since the browser folder contains no tasks sub folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 305.13,
          "end": 308.4,
          "en": "the request might fail without that setting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 308.4,
          "end": 311.64,
          "en": "So this setting is important so that Firebase makes sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 311.64,
          "end": 315.93,
          "en": "that all requests no matter which path they have reached",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 315.93,
          "end": 318.75,
          "en": "this one single HTML file and therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 318.75,
          "end": 321.06,
          "en": "the script code loaded by that file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 321.06,
          "end": 324.84,
          "en": "which then does allow the Angular router to take over",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 324.84,
          "end": 327.42,
          "en": "and handle that incoming request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 327.42,
          "end": 331.35,
          "en": "So that's an important setting that must be set to yes here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 331.35,
          "end": 334.65,
          "en": "Now here, I don't care about automatic builds and deploys,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 334.65,
          "end": 336.45,
          "en": "so choose N for no.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 336.45,
          "end": 340.83,
          "en": "And with that, finally, the initialization is done.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 340.83,
          "end": 344.43,
          "en": "Now with that, some new files have been added,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 344.43,
          "end": 347.25,
          "en": "essentially, these two Firebase files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 347.25,
          "end": 351.303,
          "en": "which contain the configuration details that we just set up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 353.37,
          "end": 356.90999999999997,
          "en": "And with that done, now finally, we're ready to deploy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 356.90999999999997,
          "end": 360.99,
          "en": "the application by running Firebase deploy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 360.99,
          "end": 365.31,
          "en": "So now, here in my terminal, I'll run that command",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 365.31,
          "end": 366.78,
          "en": "and that will now go ahead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 366.78,
          "end": 370.98,
          "en": "and deploy my build files to Firebase.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 370.98,
          "end": 373.95,
          "en": "For that to work you of course, first of all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 373.95,
          "end": 377.01,
          "en": "need to run NPM run build though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 377.01,
          "end": 379.08,
          "en": "Now, we already did that here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 379.08,
          "end": 381.57,
          "en": "but you must run the build command first",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 381.57,
          "end": 385.65,
          "en": "so that you have this dist folder which is being deployed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 385.65,
          "end": 387.003,
          "en": "That's important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 387.9,
          "end": 390.54,
          "en": "By the way, you should make sure that you don't have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 390.54,
          "end": 394.11,
          "en": "some white space here as I did initially,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 394.11,
          "end": 397.11,
          "en": "because otherwise, it will actually create a new folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 397.11,
          "end": 399.84000000000003,
          "en": "that doesn't contain your application code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 399.84000000000003,
          "end": 402.54,
          "en": "So that public folder path here really must be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 402.54,
          "end": 404.76,
          "en": "the correct path to that browser folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 404.76,
          "end": 408.33,
          "en": "without any leading white space or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 408.33,
          "end": 412.02,
          "en": "Now with that, the project will be deployed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 412.02,
          "end": 415.83,
          "en": "and as a result, you should actually already get a link here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 415.83,
          "end": 419.58,
          "en": "that allows you to visit the deployed website.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 419.58,
          "end": 423.69,
          "en": "So Firebase also automatically sets up some dummy domain",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 423.69,
          "end": 428.22,
          "en": "for you, which you can use to preview the deployed website.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 428.22,
          "end": 431.403,
          "en": "You can of course also link your own domain if you want to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 432.24,
          "end": 434.43,
          "en": "Here, I'll visit this domain though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 434.43,
          "end": 439.43,
          "en": "And there indeed I can see that this all seems to work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
